{
    "format": "jef-sure/boards",
    "format_version": 2,
    "kind": "board",
    "name": "jc8012p4a1c",
    "title": "Guition JC8012P4A1C",
    "description": "10.1-inch 800x1280 JD9365 on MIPI-DSI (lying 1280x800), GSL3680 touch (firmware written into it at start), ES8311 sound",
    "notes": [
        "BOOT (GPIO35) is under the cover.",
        "The nets named ES7210_* on the schematic are lines of the ES8311: its sheets have no ES7210 chip.",
        "A start can fail before app_main, about one in ten after a reset over USB: a store access fault while ESP-IDF sets up, or in the ROM. The chip restarts or the next start goes through. The cause is not known."
    ],
    "mcu": {
        "target": "esp32p4",
        "flash_mb": 16,
        "psram_mb": 32,
        "revision": "3.2",
        "notes": "The display reads 160 MB/s from the PSRAM within a row: at 200 MHz a moving picture leaves it short now and then and the screen flashes light blue for a frame. 250 MHz leaves it enough, so revision 3 is needed here."
    },
    "checked": {
        "pins": {"level": "schematic", "source": "JC8012P4A1.pdf, vendor archive", "date": "2026-10-28"},
        "sound": {
            "level": "hardware",
            "covers": ["devices.sound"],
            "by": "Anton",
            "date": "2026-10-31",
            "result": "confirmed",
            "notes": "hello_board through the adapter: its tone heard on the speaker of the case, quiet, at volume 25 and a quarter of full scale. Heard before in Prince of Persia of DGX-GE."
        },
        "schematic_parts": {
            "level": "schematic",
            "covers": [
                "devices.sd",
